    "lore": "From humble beginnings, the house of al-Saud became one of the dominant powers of the entire Arabian peninsula - and when World War Two changed everything, in Arabia everything stayed the same. With meetings and handshakes, the Saudi royalty kept its independence under the wings of the Italian empire - becoming the only nation in the Italian sphere not to host a garrison from Rome, all in exchange for easy access to oil. Thanks to oil deals with Italy, the Saudi house became fabulously rich, and they fully intend to put their wealth to good use. As many in the Arab and Islamic world look to Riyadh as a beacon for Muslim opposition to western imperialism, the Saudis silently bid their time, waiting for the right moment to lead the fight against the Italian oppressors, and to finally achieve their true calling as the leaders of the faithful."
